WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.149
Hi, my name is Chris Gagne and I'm an Agile Coach.

00:00:03.699 --> 00:00:09.620
Today, I'll talk about the working agreement. The working agreement is a documented set of ground rules

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:14.900
that the team creates and follows in  order to improve their productivity and happiness.

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:17.420
Think of some of the things that slow your team down.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:23.060
For example, some teams find that their meetings are more productive when everyone puts away their phones and laptops

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:30.220
unless they need them for the meeting. Other teams find that having individuals come too late to their stand up limits their usefulness.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:35.000
The best way to create a working agreement is to use a little bit of reverse psychology.

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:40.080
Get together as a team and brainstorm all the ways that your team can fail.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:48.560
Then prioritize the five most significant risks to your team based on their likelihood of occurring and the severity of their impact.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:53.800
Then come up with a specific rule that would prevent that from happening.

00:00:54.340 --> 00:01:00.560
So, for instance, perhaps the team agrees that having people working on their laptops during the meeting is a big risk to their productivity.

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:05.580
They then create a rule that says the only person would should have their laptop open

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:08.580
is the person presenting their screen to the rest of the team.

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:10.940
All other electronics should be put away.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:17.040
If there's a production issue, the person working on the issue should leave the room, so as not to distract everyone else.

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:23.340
See if you can come up with about five to seven rules to help with the top five risks you've identified,

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:26.440
then post this in a conspicuous location.

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:33.210
If you're co-located, write each role on a sticky note and paste it on the wall near your desks. If you're distributed,

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:35.670
create a page in your wiki or a similar space.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:42.060
The whole team is responsible for holding each other accountable and following the working agreement.

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:45.689
Be polite and ask each other to follow the rules that you agree to.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:48.600
Escalate only as a last resort.

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:55.120
Review your working agreement regularly, at least once every sprint at the retrospective.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:02:01.920
The team can add or remove items to the working agreement at any time, so long as there is general consensus.

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:10.820
If your team creates and uses a working agreement diligently, you will soon find that your team is happier and more productive.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.460
Best of luck!

